WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.650
m is how far the line goes up for each step to the right.

2
00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:07.703
Here m is one: one step right, and up one.

3
00:00:08.431 --> 00:00:12.131
Make m bigger: up two for each step, so the line is steeper.

4
00:00:14.685 --> 00:00:19.085
m is three: up three, and it still crosses the y axis at one.

5
00:00:21.345 --> 00:00:25.070
When m is zero, there are no steps up, so the line is flat.

6
00:00:30.486 --> 00:00:35.161
A negative m goes down: m of negative two is down two each step.
